ready: 1
kind: rule
id: recall.rule.gut-check
display_id: RULE-RECALL-GUT-CHECK
module: recall
title: When a guardrail pauses or warns before a tool call
summary: A matching guardrail pauses the first attempt of a risky action once per session, and otherwise
  warns once per session.
inputs:
- name: tool call
  source: The runtime's pre-tool hook
  source_kind: payload
- name: guardrails
  source: Active guardrail memories
  source_kind: stored
- name: session history
  source: The recall log for this session
  source_kind: stored
- name: daemon answering
  source: The hook handler's connection
  source_kind: derived
decision:
  nodes:
  - id: in
    node_kind: input
    text: One active guardrail and one planned tool call
    refs:
    - memory.data.memory
    - recall.data.recall-log
  - id: trig
    node_kind: decision
    text: Does the guardrail list any triggers?
  - id: match
    node_kind: decision
    text: Does every listed trigger match the tool name, the command text or a path in the call?
  - id: similar
    node_kind: decision
    text: Is the call close enough in meaning to the guardrail?
    refs:
    - recall.const.gut-check-similarity
  - id: bump
    node_kind: decision
    text: Is the guardrail intense enough, does it have triggers, is the daemon answering, and has this
      action not been paused this session?
    refs:
    - recall.const.speed-bump-arousal
  - id: advised
    node_kind: decision
    text: Has this guardrail already warned in this session?
  - id: speed
    node_kind: outcome
    text: Pause this attempt with the guardrail as the reason; the identical retry goes through
  - id: advise
    node_kind: outcome
    text: Show the guardrail beside the call, which proceeds
  - id: none
    node_kind: outcome
    text: Nothing
  edges:
  - from: in
    to: trig
  - from: trig
    to: match
    label: 'yes'
  - from: trig
    to: similar
    label: 'no'
  - from: match
    to: bump
    label: 'yes'
  - from: match
    to: none
    label: 'no'
  - from: similar
    to: advised
    label: 'yes'
  - from: similar
    to: none
    label: 'no'
  - from: bump
    to: speed
    label: 'yes'
  - from: bump
    to: advised
    label: 'no'
  - from: advised
    to: none
    label: 'yes'
  - from: advised
    to: advise
    label: 'no'
constants:
- recall.const.gut-check-max-warnings
- recall.const.speed-bump-arousal
- recall.const.gut-check-similarity
default: Nothing
precedence:
- When several guardrails match, at most the maximum number of warnings are kept, most intense first,
  and one pause among them decides the response.
rationale: 'A pause stops the action once and lets the identical retry through, like a gut feeling: it
  forces a second look at the moment of risk without turning one bad memory into a lost capability. Only
  guardrails with explicit triggers can pause, because similarity alone misfires. Without the daemon there
  is no session history, so a pause could repeat forever; the direct path only warns. Warning once per
  session keeps the agent from learning to ignore the warning.'
